          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 5.5: Let us investigate"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.4,
            0.682,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": " Tie an eraser (or a potato) to one end of a thread."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.426,
            0.743,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": " Hang the eraser by holding the other end of the thread (Fig. 5.16). Keep your hand steady."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.474,
            0.743,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": " Using the other hand, take the eraser slightly to one side and then release (Fig. 5.16)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.52,
            0.743,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "Does it start moving to and fro? Is its motion similar to the motion of a swing?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.566,
            0.744,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": "When an object moves to and fro about some fixed position, its motion is called **oscillatory motion.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.624,
            0.769,
            0.823
          ],
